## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Solution |
|---|---|
| Wazuh agent not connecting | Check SOC-SIEM IP in ossec.conf |
| Sysmon not collecting events | Reinstall with config file path |
| PowerShell logs not in Wazuh | Verify GPO applied, restart agent |
| VM extremely slow | Reduce RAM to 2 GB; close other VMs |
| Windows ARM image won't boot | Use UTM Windows installer wizard |

## Resource Management

| Scenario | Active VMs | Total RAM |
|---|---|---:|
| Windows testing only | SOC-SIEM + Windows-Endpoint | 6-7 GB |
| Windows attack simulation | SOC-SIEM + Windows-Endpoint + Attacker-Box | 7-8 GB (tight) |
| Combined testing | SOC-SIEM + Linux + Windows | 7-8 GB (very tight) |

**Recommendation:** Shut down Linux-Endpoint when testing Windows, and vice versa.
